{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31601 - PROTEIN:5776",
  "verbalization": "Arundinol B is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387, which is a complex molecule with multiple targets, including MIP. The evidence suggests that Arundinol B directly targets SNU-387, and SNU-387, in turn, is a target of several compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, all of which ultimately target MIP. This chain of interactions implies that Arundinol B may exert its effects through a pathway that involves SNU-387, which is a key intermediate in the targeting of MIP. The evidence supports a mechanism where Arundinol B acts as a modulator of SNU-387, which in turn influences MIP through a series of molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the biological activity of Arundinol B and its downstream effects on MIP.",
